 nights Watchmen and  horses we saw the pattern again in  season 5 when the children of the forest  created the night king and then again in  season 7 in the cave drawings at  Dragonstone we still don't know get its  significance but clearly it's an  important sign of the White Walkers in  another nod to season 1 John and arias  reunion in this episode is a close a  mirror of when John and Arya said  goodbye in season 1 episode 2 they hug  in a near identical way and that's when  John gave Arya needle her beloved sword  in this episode John notices that Arya  still has the blade  we see John fly a dragon for the first  time which is certainly momentous but  there's actually more going on here the  dragon John flies is Ragle named after  his real father Rhaegar Targaryen in the  season 8 trailer we saw this same scene  but John was not in the shot this scene  is no doubt a reference to when John  made love to his first love Ygritte in a  cave near a waterfall according to the  creators this location in season 8 is  also where John would have hunted when  he was younger  Arya meets ginjury and hands him a  drawing of a new weapon she wants him to  make out of dragonglass in the season 2  trailer we see Arya with a new dagger  which could be what she's asking ginjury  to make for her in this episode ginjury  and Arya reunite ginjury calls arya lady  Stark  - which Arya replies don't call me that  ginjury then replies as you wish milady  this is a direct mirror of a  conversation they had in season 2  episode 2 I should be called a new  milady do not call me milady  as Brady commands tyrion says because of  john's courage they have brought the  greatest army the world has ever seen  this is similar to a phrase Mance Rayder  says back in season 3 mance was talking  about lighting a fire to alert the  wildlings that it was time to attack  Castle black in the scene with bran  Qyburn gives bran a crossbow the weapons  sir she wants Bronn to use to kill her  traitor brothers this is significant  because you may remember that Tyrion  uses a crossbow to kill their father  Tywin Lannister  midway through the episode Sam finds  brand and brand says he's waiting for an  old friend we find out later the old  friend he's referring to is Jaime  Lannister who shows up at Winterfell  Jaime pushed bran out a window back in  season 1 leading to the injury that left  him unable to walk the things I do for  love  so there you have it do we miss anything  let us know in the comments  [Music]
 

